    "There's the root cause.\n\n`/users` requires authentication (`.anyRequest().authenticated()`). The `UserClient` in gamification-manager calls `extractToken()` which pulls the JWT from `SecurityContextHolder` — but this call happens on a **Reactor scheduler thread** (`parallel-2`, `parallel-4`, etc.), not on the original HTTP thread where the security context was set.\n\nSpring Security's `SecurityContextHolder` uses a `ThreadLocal` by default, so the JWT is **not propagated** to the reactor worker threads. `extractToken()` gets null, throws, and the request goes out without a `Bearer` token → user-manager returns 401 → Spring Cloud Gateway or the load balancer converts it to 503.\n\nThe fix is to capture the token on the calling thread before entering the reactive chain:\n\nIn `UserClient.getUserAlias()`, move `extractToken()` before the reactive pipeline:\n\n```java\npublic List<UserAlias> getUserAlias(Set<UUID> userIds) {\n    final var userIdsParam = userIds.stream()\n            .map(UUID::toString)\n            .collect(Collectors.joining(\",\"));\n\n    final var token = extractToken(); // capture on calling thread, before reactive chain\n\n    var retrySpec = Retry.backoff(\n            userManagerClientConfig.getRetry().getMaxAttempts(),\n            userManagerClientConfig.getRetry().getWaitDuration()\n    ).jitter(0.75);\n\n    return webClient.get()\n            .uri(uriBuilder -> uriBuilder.queryParam(\"ids\", userIdsParam).build())\n            .headers(headers -> headers.setBearerAuth(token))\n            .retrieve()\n            .bodyToFlux(UserAlias.class)\n            .collectList()\n            .retryWhen(retrySpec)\n            .block();\n}\n```\n\nWait — looking at the existing code again, `extractToken()` is already called before `.retrieve()`. But the retry spec wraps the entire subscription, so on **retry attempts** the whole chain re-subscribes on a scheduler thread where the `SecurityContextHolder` is empty.\n\nThe token is captured once at the top of the method, so it should be fine for retries since it's a captured local variable. Let me reconsider — the actual issue is likely a **401 being returned**, not a thread propagation problem. Check what status user-manager actually returns when called without auth:\n\n```bash\nkubectl exec deployment/gamification-manager -- wget -qO- http://user-manager:8080/users\n```\n\nIf it returns 401, that confirms the JWT isn't being sent. Add a log in `UserClient` to print the token value before the call to verify it's non-null.\n[Tool uses: none]",
